arabola $y={x}^{2}$ by\n\n- $h$ units right, and\n\n- $k$ units up.\n\nThe vertex of $y=(x-h)^{2}+k$ is located at $(h,k).$\n\nHere, the parabola is translated $2$ units *left*, so we have $h=-2.$ The parabola is also translated $5$ units *up*, so we have $k=5.$ \n\n![](images/8e/8e69ca48e852176d2ed258f062995835889374975492873fe0863ea782d87ebd.png)\n\nThe vertex is located at $(-2,5),$ and these are the coordinates of the minimum point."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529145 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068865 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36e2e343-4403-51b2-965f-168bbe606112" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Combination of Horizontal and Vertical Translations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04cf61b8-04db-5f45-abb5-90fdc5ad1da5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a5/a5313544206d95a45b695bfeb6bc05ced0c113fe0e64760de3c8b9f618aa3749.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528312} {:answer/id #uuid "29128bb6-698e-5f80-b2d5-1fcc609cce2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4e/4e43c68bd7ab2da6fb0be21ecc69ab29e111c442219caaae70b819e9df3488be.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528402} {:answer/id #uuid "9b46fcef-4a09-54d0-bb34-c44b26d14ef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1d/1d3505d032f9e3281f1686fc2816ceef71c97f1f886e6b720217481815d8e9ad.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528672} {:answer/id #uuid "af3ac06e-20d5-5b0d-8ed2-f6ae178a5871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d46be7b4202aecdd112ffac222098e4f50f63d637c3358f122ce66598be69a88.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528725} {:answer/id #uuid "c7a8fd16-dc61-55e3-965a-7b6d954cc4b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/67/67cffd6bf1285b40c69a58b2571d7f396cd4df34d9d7ac71925ce5b6ecc8a633.